  "headline": "Under the explicit omega-normalized Marcelis trace gauge, the 357 lines of PG(3,4) have exactly two image types in PG(3,2): 125 descend to genuine three-point binary lines, while 232 become five-point subsets spanning binary projective planes. The point map is therefore structured but not an incidence morphism.",
  "marcelis_reading": "Marcelis' GF(4)->GF(2) trace tables should be read as structured, gauge-fixed coordinate projections. Some selected GF4 lines really do descend to PG(3,2) lines, but most do not; 232/357 become punctured Fano planes. This exact census prevents promoting a useful trace dictionary into a false projective-incidence map.",
